{"title":"Career roadmap — Travel Consultant","role":"Travel Consultant","summary":"A Travel Consultant designs and sells travel solutions for individuals, families, corporates, groups, and specialised travellers. The role combines destination knowledge + itinerary planning + airline/hotel systems + customer service + sales + travel technology + commercial skills.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Com (Bachelor of Commerce)","Course":"B.Com – Travel & Tourism / Aviation"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Com graduate, the strongest advantage is combining tourism knowledge with business, finance, sales, analytics, and digital booking technology."}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Travel Consultant / Travel Executive; master reservations, itinerary planning, ticketing, customer service and travel sales"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Senior Travel Consultant / Corporate Travel Specialist; specialise in international, corporate, luxury or MICE travel"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Travel Manager / Product Manager / Travel Operations Manager; manage clients, suppliers and travel programmes"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Head of Travel / Travel Business Director / Travel Entrepreneur; lead technology-enabled travel operations and customer strategy"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Travel & business foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Tourism fundamentals"},{"text":"Geography"},{"text":"Travel industry structure"},{"text":"Tourism economics"},{"text":"Hospitality fundamentals"},{"text":"Airline industry basics"},{"text":"Hotel operations"},{"text":"Travel documentation"},{"text":"Business communication"},{"text":"Customer relationship management"},{"text":"Account