n","0–2 Years: Travel Executive / Consultant","2–5 Years: Senior Consultant / Destination Specialist","5–8 Years: Travel Manager / Product Manager","8–15 Years: Head of Travel / Business Director","15+ Years: Travel Business Leader / Entrepreneur"],"label":"Year 1"},{"type":"h","text":"Best employability combination"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Com Travel & Tourism","Travel Internship","GDS","Airline/Hotel Reservations","Itinerary Planning","Sales","Excel","CRM","Travel Documentation","Corporate/Luxury/MICE Specialisation","AI Travel Technology"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"note","label":"Key principle","text":"A strong Travel Consultant is not merely a ticket or hotel booking agent. The valuable professional can understand the traveller's needs, design a practical experience, optimise cost and time, manage suppliers, handle disruptions, and create enough trust that customers return for future travel."}]}]}